# Cloudflare Workers static-assets header rules (limit: 100 rules).
#
# IMPORTANT — how CSP is split here:
# Astro emits a <meta> CSP carrying per-build SHA-256 hashes for inline
# scripts and styles (security.csp in astro.config.mjs). When a page is
# covered by two policies, BOTH are enforced independently and content must
# satisfy each one. So this file must NOT set default-src, script-src or
# style-src: doing so would block hash-allowed inline content that the meta
# policy correctly permits, because the hashes only exist in the meta tag.
#
# That constraint rules out default-src, which is the usual way to cover the
# remaining fetch directives. So they are enumerated explicitly below instead.
# None of them interact with hashes, so they are safe to set here. Verified
# against the built output before adding: the site loads no data: URIs, no
# audio or video, no iframes, no web workers and no manifest, and its only
# fetch() is Astro's prefetch module, which checks location.origin before
# firing. The links to GitHub and LinkedIn are anchors, not subresources, so
# no fetch directive applies to them.
#
# These are deliberately strict. If a future page needs an external image, an
# embedded video or a manifest, it will fail visibly in the console and the
# directive should be widened by hand rather than loosened pre-emptively.
#
# Still uncovered, and unavoidable: <link rel="prefetch"> falls back to
# default-src, and prefetch-src is deprecated and gone from current browsers.
# It is same-origin only, per the origin check above.
#
# This file therefore carries the directives a <meta> CSP cannot express
# (frame-ancestors, report-to, sandbox) plus every directive that never
# interacts with hashes.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; media-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'; manifest-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# Astro fingerprints these filenames, so they are safe to cache forever.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The PDF CV is regenerated each build; let it revalidate.
/cv/*.pdf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate
